  "title": "S4 v2: enable the claude:opus executor row and [models].opus = claude-opus-5-5; test harness drops live claude rows",
  "spec": "Respec of T-1370 (its gate failed because tests/_harness.py copies the live pool.toml and 12 tests assume Codex-only executors; fix rounds could not extend its write scope). Goal T-1334, config + test harness on the goal branch; the row activates when the goal PR merges into main.\nYou may start from commit 01552aea385823f797ad308e3f2b5c58912883f2 (branch task/T-1370: the pool.toml row + test) with git cherry-pick, then:\n1. .orchestrator/pool.toml: [models] opus = \"claude-opus-5-5\" (comment: 2026-09-23 user: Opus 5.5 for the opus tier and the claude:opus executor row; revert: \"claude-opus-5\"); after the last [[executors]] row add id = \"claude:opus\", provider = \"claude\", roles = [\"execute\"], complexity_min = 1, complexity_max = 10, max_parallel = 2 (comment: keep small, [limits].max_parallel_claude_workers not yet enforced for routed Claude executes), daily_budget_tasks = 20, quota_group = \"claude\", weight = 1.0, enabled = true (comment: goal T-1334; revert: enabled = false).\n2. tests/_harness.py: in the section-split loop that copies pool.toml into the TMP root (tests/_harness.py:11-20), drop every [[executors]] section whose body has provider = \"claude\"; comment: live routed Claude rows are an operator setting; tests that need one build it.\n3. tests/test_pool.py::test_shipped_pool_toml_claude_opus_row_is_valid: load REPO/.orchestrator/pool.toml (REPO from _harness) with tomllib, build Pool(cfg=that dict), assert executor \"claude:opus\" exists, provider \"claude\", enabled True, model == cfg[\"models\"][\"opus\"] == \"claude-opus-5-5\"; independent of the TMP copy.\nNo other changes; the 12 tests that failed in the T-1370 gate must pass unedited.",
